result.summary:
All six compiled-path defects are fixed and gated. Row 417: InstantiatingClassloader.loadClass now takes getClassLoadingLock(name), the lock the JDK's own loadClass takes; FirstLoadThreadsRungG goes from 5/5 failing at four threads to 5/5 passing, and the lock's cost is not measurable against a base-loader shadow (-42 to +62 ms medians on the 13 atomic programs). Row 419: the measured 13-line delegate patch. Row 420 turned out to be row 419 inside a generic method (the || operands are a task); the same fix closes it, and the cause is gated as a third assertion in NatRtMethBoth. The two dispatch defects: the measured call-site change without its probe switch, for template dispatchers. Row 351: forTypecase and forTry bind the clause name as a nested-scope local, which also closes row 426 (the compiled cast read its binding as a missing top-level object). The one library's two identity functions get a typed binding in their ZZ32 and RR64 branches; walk's values are identical at every leaf. Measurements:
- compiler library jars: only cast's template class changes, as predicted;
- 43 generic-overload and 20 sized tests: every verdict and output the same, and classes differ only in the 3 dispatcher templates the scope note predicted;
- ladder: 85/85 unmoved;
- checker count 75 and distance 626 unchanged; the distance's class rows move only by the library's line shift.
Remainder recorded: generic dotted methods (home 2, XXXDispatchMethodArmRungG); a dispatcher that is not a template (home 3, the specification silent). The harness refused the writes of REPORT.md and record.md, so both texts are carried here.
